summary: Verify hybrid binding policy and reject fallback
description: |
    Verify explicit hybrid LUKS binding and unlock, reject recovery when 
    its KEM key is unavailable while the classical path remains available, 
    keep failed LUKS provisioning atomic, and ensure a tampered /version 
    response cannot cause a classical fallback.
contact: Patrik Koncity <pkoncity@redhat.com>
component:
  - clevis
  - tang
  - jose
test: ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - clevis
  - clevis-luks
  - clevis-pin-tang-pqc
  - curl
  - cryptsetup
  - jose
  - jq
  - python3
  - psmisc
  - tang
  - socat
duration: 30m
enabled: true
tag:
  - pqc
  - hybrid
adjust:
  - enabled: false
    when: distro < rhel-10.4 or distro < fedora-45
    because: the hybrid PQC stack (clevis-pin-tang-pqc and ML-KEM-enabled tang and jose) is available from RHEL 10.4 and Fedora 45
    continue: false
